  "description": "T1: Lime tree (Tilia species) - Fell to ground level and remove all arisings, including stump grinding to below ground level.\r\rT2: Portuguese Laurel (Prunus lusitanica) - Fell to ground level and remove all arisings, including stump grinding to below ground level.\r\rReason for Works:\rThe trees are located at the end of the rear garden and their removal is required to facilitate appropriate use and management of the garden space. The trees significantly reduce natural light to the property and neighbouring dwellings. In addition, the lime tree produces sap which affects neighbouring properties, and extended branches have enabled wildlife, including squirrels, to access adjacent buildings, causing disturbance to neighbouring homes."
